          "quote": "11.6 Return of Confidential Information. Upon the effective date of the termination of this Agreement for any reason in its entirety, or with respect to a Product, either Party may request in writing and the non-requesting Party shall (at the non-requesting Party's election), with respect to Confidential Information to which such non-requesting Party does not retain rights under the surviving provisions of this Agreement (if applicable, with respect to the terminated Region or terminated Product) promptly destroy all copies of such Confidential Information in the possession or control of the non-requesting Party and confirm such destruction in writing",
          "rationale": "The Agreement contains a full exit/transition architecture, so no clause is missing. Section 11.6 gives a mutual, on-request return/destruction-with-written-certification mechanic for Confidential Information (with reasonable archival/back-up carve-outs), which is the data-return element the rule seeks and is not an immediate-deletion walk-away. Section 12.3 sets out detailed wind-down mechanics: transfer of Regulatory Approvals, Regulatory Materials, clinical and pharmacovigilance data within fixed periods (12.3(c)(iv), (d)(iii)), a defined Transition Assistance package including technical assistance and Know-How transfer for a stated post-termination period (12.3(c)(vi)C), inventory sell-off and transition services (12.3(c)(iii), (vi)G), and RevMed-side assistance to Sanofi on a Change of Control termination (12.3(e)); Section 7.2 obliges RevMed to transfer Manufacturing Know-How to Sanofi on request. Direction is structurally reversed from a typical hosting deal: because rights in the Products revert to RevMed on termination, most transition duties properly run from Sanofi to RevMed, so those obligations are the bargained reversion consideration rather than a rule breach and we do not flag them. Noted but not flagged: the durations are redacted ([***]) so we cannot confirm a 90-day/6-month floor, and Section 7.2 is not listed in the Section 12.4 survival list, so post-expiry manufacturing know-how support is not expressly preserved. Overall the clause set meets or exceeds the fallback position.",
